# Vocabulary coverage

## List markers

- dash
* star
. auto-numbered
1. decimal period
1) decimal paren
1)) decimal parens
a. lower alpha period
a) lower alpha paren
a: lower alpha parens
A. upper alpha period
A) upper alpha paren
A: upper alpha parens
i. lower roman period
i) lower roman paren
i: lower roman parens
I. upper roman period
I) upper roman paren
I: upper roman parens

## Comment fences

%%% TODO
The info string on the fence opener is its own node.
%%%

## Breaks

A backslash before a space is a hard break, as here: a \ b
and the paragraph carries on.

## Reserved container sigils

::: >
A quote written as a container.

:::

::: |
A line block.

:::

::: \
A local hard break block.

:::

::: figure
A composite figure.

:::

## Tables

| a | b |
+ continued | d |
|{.x} attributed | plain |
|=>{.y} aligned | b |

^ A caption with content.

## Inline

![alt][ref] is a full reference image and ![alt][] is a collapsed one.

!`html`{=html} is not the raw inline form. The raw inline form is spelled with
braces: {=html}<b>verbatim</b>{=html}, and the format name is its own node.

## Continuation marker

> Quoted prose.
+
The block below attaches to the quote without a marker prefix.
